      "fact_text": {
        "text": "To declare an array of integers, place square brackets after the type name (e.g., int[]).",
        "refs": ["Q0000"]
      },
      "fact_type": null
    },
    {
      "fact_text": {
        "text": "Arrays are reference types; they must be instantiated with the new operator.",
        "refs": ["Q0000"]
      },
      "fact_type": null
    },
    {
      "fact_text": {
        "text": "When creating an array, the size (length) is specified in square brackets after the new operator.",
        "refs": ["Q0001"]
      },
      "fact_type": null
    },
    {
      "fact_text": {
        "text": "Variable names should reflect that they hold a list of items (e.g., numbers instead of number).",
        "refs": ["Q0001"]
      },
      "fact_type": null
    },
    {
      "fact_text": {
        "text": "Array elements are accessed using the variable name followed by the index in square brackets (e.g., numbers[0]).",
        "refs": ["Q0002"]
      },
      "fact_type": null
    },
    {
      "fact_text": {
        "text": "Printing an array directly yields a string based on the object's memory address, not its contents.",
        "refs": ["Q0003"]
      },
      "fact_type": null
    },
